🚀 Part 2: Roadmap — What Next Steps to Take
Based on what you've already built and your vision, here's a phased roadmap:

Phase 2: Technical/Chart Analysis Layer 🔜 (Next)
You already have ta in your requirements and price history. Build on this:

Technical indicators: Moving Averages (SMA/EMA), RSI, MACD, Bollinger Bands, VWAP
Chart pattern detection: Support/resistance levels, trend lines
Store computed indicators in PostgreSQL for historical analysis
Frontend: Interactive candlestick charts with overlays (use a charting library like Lightweight Charts or ngx-charts for Angular)
Phase 3: External World / Sentiment Layer 🌍
This is where your project becomes truly unique:

News Sentiment Analysis:
Use free news APIs (Polygon.io news, NewsAPI, or GNews)
Run NLP sentiment analysis (HuggingFace's finbert model — purpose-built for financial text)
Store sentiment scores per stock per day
Macro-Economic Indicators:
Fetch interest rates, inflation (CPI), GDP data from FRED API (free, by the US Federal Reserve)
For India-specific: RBI data, sectoral indices from NSE
Insider/Institutional Activity:
Track FII/DII data (can be scraped from NSE/BSE)
Correlate with price movements
Phase 4: AI-Powered Analysis & Suggestions 🤖
This is the crown jewel of your vision:

Scoring Engine:
Combine fundamental score (from your existing metrics) + technical score + sentiment score → Composite Stock Health Score
AI Summarizer:
Use an LLM (OpenAI API, or free alternatives like Groq/Mistral) to generate natural-language stock reports
Input: fundamentals JSON + technical indicators + news sentiment
Output: "RELIANCE shows strong revenue growth of 12% YoY, but RSI at 78 indicates overbought territory. Recent news sentiment is neutral. Consider waiting for a pullback."
Anomaly Detection:
Use scikit-learn (already in your requirements!) to detect unusual volume spikes, price deviations from historical patterns
Phase 5: User Experience & Portfolio 👤
User Authentication (JWT-based)
Watchlists & Portfolio Tracking
Custom Alerts (price targets, fundamental thresholds)
Stock Screener with multi-parameter filtering
Comparison Dashboard (you already have sector_comparision.py — expand this)
Phase 6: Production Hardening 🛡️
Caching layer (Redis) for frequently accessed data
Rate limit management across multiple API providers
Data quality checks and reconciliation between providers
Deployment (Docker + cloud hosting)
